; NextDAAD sprites-under-audio fixture. STIMULUS fixture: tests\build-tests.ps1
; asserts the compiled bytes; tests\spraud_dump.py drives it over ZRCP and
; reads the DEBUG sprite snapshot after every step. Staged by
; tests\build-tests.ps1 -SprAud into sd\SPRAUD\ with 002/006/020/021.ANI,
; 006.AKY (the kit's 9-channel tune, SongToAky of authoring-kit\AUDIO\1.aks),
; 001.WAV (440 Hz, 16000 bytes) and 002.WAV (880 Hz, 12000 bytes), both under
; SFX_WIN_BYTES so they take the COMPLETE arm, and 003.WAV (220 Hz, 40000
; bytes, STREAMING arm).
;
; A5-A9 (every sampled effect) are SILICON-ONLY. sfx_stream_open counts the
; DISK_FILEMAP runs by subtracting 6 from the returned byte count until zero;
; ZEsarUX's esxDOS handler returns an ODD count (HL sampled dc53, 4fc1, 7e83
; with DE 6), so the loop never ends there and the fixture parks in
; SFX_STREAM_OPEN@COUNT. CSpect cannot be driven by a reader. So the walk puts
; the emulator-provable steps first - scene, music, restart under music,
; music stop - and tests\spraud_dump.py stops at A4.
;
; Four sets that share the screen without a palette-block clash: 002 torch
; (8-bit, block 15) and its copies 020/021, plus 006 (4-bit, blocks 1 and 2).
; 003 and 018 are NOT usable here - 003's green is index $1C in block 1 and
; 018 claims blocks 1 and 2, both refused while 006 runs. Every sprite sits
; in the left half of the display, clear of the right-hand text window.
;
; A2, A6 and A8 wait in the GETMS tracking loop (MOUSE 104 3 + INKEY + SKIP,
; PAUSE 25 debounce) so the tester can move the pointer under the audio;
; every other step keeps ANYKEY. Flags 100-103 feed GFX 100 20; 104-107 are
; GETMS. The restarts (A3, A7) put 020 and 021 back at their flag positions,
; not their file position: three identical torches on one spot read as one,
; so a refused restart would be invisible. 006 restarts before 002 so the
; channel order flips and the reader can see the restart happened.

/CTL
_
/VOC
NORTH  2  noun
SOUTH  3  noun
LOOK   4  verb
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I can't do that."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 "Press any key.#n"
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "A1 four sets, silence#n"
/1 "A2 SFX 6 7 music loops - move the mouse#n"
/2 "A3 stop-all and restart of all four under music#n"
/3 "A4 SFX 0 8 music stops, sets keep running#n"
/4 "A5 SFX 6 7 + SFX 1 1 one-shot sample over music#n"
/5 "A6 SFX 2 2 looped sample over music - hold, move the mouse#n"
/6 "A7 stop-all and restart of all four under music + loop#n"
/7 "A8 SFX 3 2 streamed loop over music - hold a minute, move the mouse#n"
/8 "A9 SFX 0 5 and SFX 0 8: silence, sets keep running#n"
/OTX
/0 "a brass lamp"
/LTX
/0 ""
/1 "The sprite lab."
/CON
/0
NORTH 1
/1
SOUTH 0
/OBJ
/0    1   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   _ _
/PRO 0
> _ _   MOUSE 0 0
        WINAT 4 40
        WINSIZE 24 40
        CLS
        MOUSE 0 1
        GFX 2 19
        GFX 6 19
        LET 100 20
        LET 101 100
        LET 102 0
        LET 103 40
        GFX 100 20
        LET 100 21
        LET 101 60
        LET 103 110
        GFX 100 20
        MESSAGE 0
        ANYKEY
        SFX 6 7
        MESSAGE 1

$poll1
> _ _   MOUSE 104 3
        INKEY
        SKIP $next1
> _ _   SKIP $poll1

$next1
> _ _   PAUSE 25
        GFX 255 21
        GFX 6 19
        GFX 2 19
        LET 100 20
        LET 101 100
        LET 103 40
        GFX 100 20
        LET 100 21
        LET 101 60
        LET 103 110
        GFX 100 20
        MESSAGE 2
        ANYKEY
        SFX 0 8
        MESSAGE 3
        ANYKEY
        SFX 6 7
        SFX 1 1
        MESSAGE 4
        ANYKEY
        SFX 2 2
        MESSAGE 5

$poll2
> _ _   MOUSE 104 3
        INKEY
        SKIP $next2
> _ _   SKIP $poll2

$next2
> _ _   PAUSE 25
        GFX 255 21
        GFX 6 19
        GFX 2 19
        LET 100 20
        LET 101 100
        LET 103 40
        GFX 100 20
        LET 100 21
        LET 101 60
        LET 103 110
        GFX 100 20
        MESSAGE 6
        ANYKEY
        SFX 0 5
        SFX 3 2
        MESSAGE 7

$poll3
> _ _   MOUSE 104 3
        INKEY
        SKIP $next3
> _ _   SKIP $poll3

$next3
> _ _   PAUSE 25
        SFX 0 5
        SFX 0 8
        MESSAGE 8
        ANYKEY
        END
/END
